    "field": "Low-cloud feedbacks",
    "problem": "Climate model simulations of tropical low-cloud response to warming vary widely, creating a major uncertainty in climate projections and motivating alternative observational approaches to predict low-cloud feedbacks.",
    "method": "This paper reviews an observational approach to predict low-cloud feedbacks by combining the observed sensitivities of clouds to their \"cloud-controlling factors\" with climate model projections of how those factors change, assuming the sensitivities are invariant across time-scales.",
    "task": "The task is to predict tropical low-cloud feedbacks by reviewing an observational approach that combines the observed sensitivity of clouds to environmental factors with model predictions of how these factors will change with warming.",
